 {"id": "QA-WARPFS-029", "title": "[QA][P3] test isolation: 4 tests assume a clean ancestor chain and break on hosts where /tmp carries a stray .vfs (3 hilo-cli cli tests + 1 hilo-metadata sidecar test fail under TMPDIR=/tmp after DF-WARPFS-161 unified graph root selection)", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": null, "blocks": null, "primary_model": "deepseek-v4-flash", "fallback_model": "deepseek-v4-flash", "reasoning": "Foreman tick warpfs-foreman-2026-10-31-13-15-07 discovered while verifying DF-WARPFS-161: with the unified manifest-boundary root selection and the no-complete-warm gate moved to the resolved root, scratch-dir tests under TMPDIR=/tmp resolve root=/tmp on hosts where a stray /tmp/.vfs exists (this host: corrupt non-UTF-8 manifest.yaml + 274KB graph.db from dogfood runs). Failing: graph_accepts_file_prefixed_path_and_teaches_id_forms, graph_impact_nonexistent_file_errors, graph_stats_no_data_prints_message (all hilo-cli/tests/cli.rs, stderr: 'No complete graph warm found. Run `hilo graph warm` first (project root: /tmp)') and sidecar::tests::find_workspace_root_none_outside_workspace (hilo-metadata, untouched by the change, asserts None got Some(\"/tmp\") \u2014 independent proof of the residue class). The same suite is green under clean-root TMPDIR (/var/tmp/hermes-scratch) and in CI. Pre-fix base passes the 3 cli tests under /tmp only because its assertions are root-agnostic (warm gate at cwd, stats cwd-local) \u2014 they predate the unified-root policy.", "capability_tags": ["qa", "test-isolation", "graph", "residue"], "worker_status": "pending", "attempts": 0, "commit_hash": null, "files_changed": null, "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": null, "created_at": "2026-10-31T19:30:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T07:52:08Z", "foreman_note": "Filed from warpfs-foreman-2026-10-31-13-15-07 verification evidence: /tmp/warpfs-161-full-tests-3.log (TMPDIR=/tmp run), /tmp/warpfs-161-full-tests-4.log (clean-root run, 67 targets green + dfwarpfs30 env class), /tmp/warpfs-161-base-proof.log (base 355c85ad passes the 3 cli tests under TMPDIR=/tmp \u2014 root-agnostic assertions). Decide the product contract for uninitialized trees under a stray ancestor: (a) isolate fixtures from ancestor residue, (b) ignore unparseable ancestor manifests as boundaries and drop cache-only fallback, or (c) adopt the acceptance transparency message 'using workspace root <abs path> (ancestor manifest)' and update tests to the ancestor-aware contract. Whatever is chosen must keep the DF-WARPFS-161 live A/B repro green.\n\nQA tick warpfs-qa-2026-11-09-00-02-10 (2026-11-09) recurrence at tested SHA 0dd62c47, and the premise widens: this run had TMPDIR pointed at a fresh tick-unique directory, so the stray-/tmp-.vfs arm was excluded, and the suite still failed exactly this way - the leak is not confined to TMPDIR. Runner-exact command 'cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast' gave 3 failures, all in this family: (1) hilo-cli cli graph_stats_no_data_prints_message - expected 'Graph cache is empty', got 'Total edges: 29 / Total files: 2' plus a component census of the operator's HOME (.hermes, duckbrain, worktrees, .cargo, ...), i.e. the test read a graph store and a scan root outside its own temp dir; (2) hilo-cli cli graph_accepts_file_prefixed_path_and_teaches_id_forms - 'DuckDB error: Binder Error: Referenced column \"granularity\" not found in FROM clause', i.e. it opened a pre-GAP-121 cache from the same HOME store; (3) hilo-metadata lib sidecar::tests::find_workspace_root_none_outside_workspace - the 'no workspace outside' test found one because the process ran under a HOME ancestor that carries workspace state. Hosted CI is green at the same SHA (run 42477564871) because a CI runner has no such state, so the product is fine and the tests are what depend on host state - the same isolation contract this row owns. The stale-cache half is filed separately as QA-WARPFS-037 because a real user with an existing cache hits it without any test involved (read-only open skips the migration).\n\ntick warpfs-qa-2026-11-09-00-02-10 cycle 3 (controller off-battery control; product tree unchanged since the battery at 0dd62c47; evidence sha256 39a6d13dd9f0d74759f678cd4cc18bcb54c9cd223b4f2525d35f5223c3bc52cb). MEASURED CONTROL that corrects the cycle-1/2 \"operator HOME cache\" attribution: with HOME pointed at an empty directory the failure PERSISTS \u2014 graph_stats_no_data_prints_message rc=101, 1 failed / 84 filtered out, and the product censused 829 components and 29 edges from /home/kara (assertion at hilo-cli/tests/cli.rs:416). So HOME is not the vector. The vector is the one this row already names: unique_tempdir() resolves through std::env::temp_dir() (hilo-cli/tests/cli.rs:135-144) and hilo selects the graph root from the ancestor chain, so any TMPDIR beneath /home/kara inherits the operator tree; a host whose temp dir sits under an unrelated populated ancestor fails the same way. Hosted CI run 42477564871 is green at 0dd62c47, the clean-machine contrast. The TMPDIR-outside-/home/kara arm is UNVERIFIED: its build was I/O-starved (cc1plus processes in D-state), so no verdict is claimed for it. No new row \u2014 recurrence of this defect, not a sibling.\n\n[cycle 4, warpfs-qa-2026-11-09-00-02-10] ATTRIBUTION CORRECTED at product level. Cycle 3 recorded the vector as \"TMPDIR ancestry\". Exact path: resolve_graph_query_root (hilo-cli/src/commands/graph.rs:1929-1945) adopts the nearest ANCESTOR that holds .vfs/graph/graph.db or .vfs/graph/edges.jsonl when no ancestor carries a manifest; this host has a stray 1.8 MB /home/kara/.vfs/graph/graph.db (2026-09-11) and no /home/kara/.vfs/manifest.yaml, so any temp dir under $HOME resolves its query root to /home/kara. Measured with target/release/hilo v0.3.0-818-ga046c89f (product-identical to tested tree 0dd62c47): in an empty temp dir under $HOME, \"hilo graph stats\" rc=0 printed \"Total edges: 29 / Total files: 2 / Components (831 total)\" with \".hermes: 2583305 files\" and \"duckbrain: 520990 files\" in ~10 min; the same run with TMPDIR=/var/tmp/hermes-scratch printed \"Graph cache is empty. Query a file or run `hilo graph warm` to populate.\" A synthetic ancestor holding only an empty edges.jsonl (no manifest) is also adopted, so the branch \u2014 not this host's cache \u2014 is the trigger. This settles the isolation arm left UNVERIFIED by cycle 3 without a build (artifacts c4-armA.out / c4-armB.out / c4-armC.out). The product half is filed separately as DF-WARPFS-161-R2 because a real user hits it with no test involved.\n\ncycle:4 warpfs-qa-2026-11-11-04-58-53: the ancestor-dependence is not /tmp-only \u2014 it also bites under $HOME, and it takes the WHOLE cli suite down. Same binary at b345275: with TMPDIR=<dir under $HOME> cli.rs = 83/85 (graph_accepts_file_prefixed_path_and_teaches_id_forms, graph_impact_nonexistent_file_errors, graph_stats_no_data_prints_message) and hilo-metadata's sidecar::tests::find_workspace_root_none_outside_workspace fails (it sees /home/kara/.vfs); with TMPDIR=/var/tmp/hermes-scratch the same binaries are 85/85 and 39/39. Fix must make tests hermetic (own root per test, no ancestor walk) rather than depending on a clean host.", "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "acceptance": "PASS: on a host carrying a stray unparseable /tmp/.vfs (corrupt manifest.yaml + graph.db), `TMPDIR=/tmp cargo test --workspace` is green including the 4 named tests, while the DF-WARPFS-161 live A/B shape still passes (nested initialized tree wins over the garbage ancestor; uninitialized-tree semantics documented); the chosen semantics for uninitialized trees under stray ancestors is written into docs/graph-engine.md. Verify: create the stray /tmp/.vfs fixture on a clean host, run `TMPDIR=/tmp cargo test -p hilo-cli --test cli` and `cargo test -p hilo-metadata --lib`, then run the DF-WARPFS-161 repro (hilo init in a nested scratch tree under a garbage-ancestor root, hilo graph impact on one of its files).", "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: the affected CLI and metadata tests pass with a stray ancestor `.vfs` present and with a clean temporary root; verify with `cargo test -p hilo_cli` and `cargo test -p hilo_metadata`, expecting exit 0 in both root conditions."}
