 {"id": "RELEASE-016", "type": "task", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "title": "Clean-machine install receipt for the v0.4.1 asset (host disk gate clear 2026-11-10; receipt must name the libfuse3 prerequisite)", "detail": "The 0.4.0 tarball is verified only on the machine that built it. The clean-machine battery (QA-WARPFS-025, QA-WARPFS-DOCS-1) was blocked while the shared bunker host's root filesystem was exhausted (100% used, 0 avail on 2026-10-20; 98% on 2026-11-03); that condition is GONE \u2014 live probe 2026-11-10: `bunker status --server bunker-mvp` -> ONLINE, uptime 4d13h32m, Agents 2/50, Disk 37% (55.2 GB/149.9 GB), 13 containers, and `ssh bunker-mvp 'df -h /'` -> /dev/sda1 150G 56G used 89G avail 39% (RC 0). The launch gate is therefore clear and this row is dispatchable now. Needed: a container/host that has never built Hilo, then download the published asset, `sha256sum -c`, `./hilo --version`, `hilo init` in an empty dir, and `hilo graph warm` on a small tree; attach the transcript to the release so the asset carries an install receipt, not just a build receipt.", "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: an evidence file records, from a machine with no prior Hilo build, the commands `gh release download v0.4.0`, `sha256sum -c hilo-0.4.0-x86_64-linux.tar.gz.sha256`, `./hilo --version` and `./hilo init` with their outputs, all exit 0, and the file is linked from the v0.4.0 release notes or a follow-up comment; the receipt also names the asset's runtime prerequisite \u2014 the v0.4.0 binary is dynamically linked against libfuse3.so.4 (ldd, measured 2026-11-09) and the tarball ships only README.md, LICENSE and hilo, so a machine without fuse3 installed cannot start it.", "reasoning": "v0.4.0 ships a prebuilt binary for the first time; without a clean-machine run the release proves only that the build host can run what it built.", "depends_on": null, "blocks": null, "attempts": 0, "created_at": "2026-11-09T16:05:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-15T22:44:47Z", "foreman_note": "Add to the clean-machine receipt (measured 2026-11-09 by releng pass 4 on the downloaded asset): the v0.4.0 binary is dynamically linked against libfuse3.so.4 (ldd), so a machine without fuse3 installed cannot start it, and the tarball ships only README.md, LICENSE and hilo - no dependency note. The receipt must name the runtime prerequisite, not just prove the checksum.\n\nRELENG PREMISE CORRECTION 2026-11-14T23:48Z (verify-only sweep): this row pins the v0.4.0 asset, but v0.4.1 has been the current release since 2026-11-12 and is not superseded (remote tag peels to 4216c7f; Release object carries hilo-0.4.1-x86_64-linux.tar.gz 32735042 B uploaded and hilo-0.4.1-x86_64-linux.tar.gz.sha256 178 B uploaded). Retarget the receipt to the v0.4.1 asset before dispatch: gh release download v0.4.1 -> sha256sum -c hilo-0.4.1-x86_64-linux.tar.gz.sha256 -> ./hilo --version -> ./hilo init, on a machine with no prior Hilo build, and keep the libfuse3 prerequisite in the receipt. A receipt produced against v0.4.0 would certify an asset nobody installs and would not satisfy the row's own purpose.\n\nRETARGETED 2026-11-15T22:44:38Z by releng tick warpfs-releng-2026-11-15-22-01-35 (second fire): the title named the superseded v0.4.0 asset. v0.4.1 is the published release (GitHub Release object published 2026-11-12T19:30:34Z, not draft, not prerelease) with assets hilo-0.4.1-x86_64-linux.tar.gz (32,735,042 bytes) and hilo-0.4.1-x86_64-linux.tar.gz.sha256 (178 bytes), both state=uploaded as read from the GitHub Releases API at 2026-11-15T22:44:38Z. A v0.4.0 install receipt would certify an asset that is no longer current, so the scope is re-anchored to v0.4.1. Scope otherwise unchanged: produce a clean-machine install receipt for the v0.4.1 asset, naming the libfuse3 prerequisite."}
