 {"id": "DF-WARPFS-161-R2-R2", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 3, "title": "[QA][P3] RECURRENCE of DF-WARPFS-161-R2 (closed complete without running its own acceptance leg): cache-only ancestor fallback still adopts a stray ~/.vfs/graph as the query root at b345275 \u2014 graph stats in an empty dir under $HOME exits 0, takes 12s, prints an 873-component census of the home tree, and never names the root", "detail": {"fingerprint": "1a468591b540a864be279559b302b3998b8204762f2e33703a28d6f06d159f87", "evidence": [{"run_id": "warpfs-qa-2026-11-11-04-58-53", "ts": "2026-11-11T07:40:42Z", "tree_fp": "4004f9d82342b75abe88293cc69d1a67448e6f606194a034a6a95b0b8449a169"}]}, "acceptance_criteria": "1) resolve_graph_query_root (hilo-cli/src/commands/graph.rs) stops adopting a bare ancestor cache that has no project boundary in the same directory: either the cache fallback requires manifest.yaml beside the cache, or it is bounded so it cannot cross into an unrelated tree; in both cases the resolved root is named on stderr (or in the message) by every graph query verb.\n2) ARM A (the leg DF-WARPFS-161-R2 never ran): on a host carrying a stray ~/.vfs/graph/graph.db (1.8 MB, no ~/.vfs/manifest.yaml), `hilo graph stats` executed from a fresh EMPTY directory under $HOME prints \"Graph cache is empty. Query a file or run `hilo graph warm` to populate.\" (or an equivalent no-root message naming the resolved root), exits 0, completes in under 2 seconds, and outputs NO component census of the home tree, no \".hermes\"/\"worktrees\"/\"duckbrain\" lines, and no \"Total edges: 29\".\n3) ARM C regression test (beside graph_query_root_prefers_nested_project_boundary): an ancestor holding ONLY .vfs/graph/edges.jsonl with no manifest.yaml must NOT be adopted \u2014 the query prints the no-root message, not \"Graph cache is empty. No edges parsed yet.\". The test must construct that fixture itself rather than depend on host residue.\n4) CLOSURE EVIDENCE: the row is closed only with the verbatim ARM A command + output pasted in the note (e.g. `cd $(mktemp -d) && time hilo graph stats`, run under $HOME on this host), PLUS `cargo test --workspace` green. A grep of the function name and the existing boundary test alone are NOT evidence for this row \u2014 that is exactly how -R2 was closed complete while the defect stayed live.", "reasoning": "REOPEN-CLASS RECURRENCE, reproduced at the tested tree b345275 (product tree == origin/master; only .gitreins/tasks.yaml differs) with the binary built from that exact tree (target/debug/hilo, \"hilo 0.4.0 / build: v0.4.0-32-gb345275-dirty\").\n\nWHY THIS IS A RECURRENCE AND NOT A SIBLING: DF-WARPFS-161-R2 was flipped to complete on 2026-11-10 by a PM verify whose evidence was (a) grep -n 'resolve_graph_query_root' and (b) cargo test -p hilo-cli graph_query_root_prefers_nested_project_boundary. Both legs exercise only the MANIFEST arm (an ancestor that carries manifest.yaml). No commit in the repo implements the cache-only arm of that row's own acceptance criteria (git log --grep='161-R2' shows only board-only commits: b344319, 5f34bd9, 7df7299, fcb666f; the only graph root change since 11-08 is da61457, which is DF-WARPFS-79-R2's remedy message). So the row closed with acceptance leg #2 never executed, and it fails live.\n\nMECHANISM (source read at b345275, hilo-cli/src/commands/graph.rs:1929-1957): resolve_graph_query_root() first looks for an ancestor carrying guard::manifest_path(dir); when NO ancestor carries a manifest it falls back to `cwd.ancestors().find(|dir| dir/.vfs/graph/graph.db exists || dir/.vfs/graph/edges.jsonl exists)` and adopts that directory as the project root. Any directory under a tree that holds a bare .vfs/graph cache therefore answers queries from that unrelated tree, with rc=0 and no diagnostic naming the root. This host carries a stray /home/kara/.vfs/graph/graph.db (1.8 MB, mtime 2026-09-11) with no /home/kara/.vfs/manifest.yaml.\n\nMEASURED AT b345275 (controller legs, artifacts kept under /home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/warpfs-qa-2026-11-11-04-58-53/c3/):\n- ARM A (acceptance leg #2): fresh empty mkdir under $HOME, no manifest, no .vfs of its own -> `hilo graph stats` rc=0 in 12.01s wall (maxrss 62 MB) printing \"Total edges: 29 / Total files: 2 / Components (873 total):\" then \".hermes: 3348032 files, 0 edges / worktrees: 544694 / duckbrain: 521188 / .duckbrain-live: 464979 / .local: 417437 ...\" \u2014 a census of the operator home tree, 12x the row's 2-second bound, with no root named. sha256 4004f9d82342b75abe88293cc69d1a67448e6f606194a034a6a95b0b8449a169 (armA2.out), fd23af22d101d2b44d2c9aa07c612a9a57c28f09ea9999cbd11a3a299e5b5aef (armA.out, same answer on the first run).\n- ARM B (control, same binary): fresh empty mkdir OUTSIDE $HOME (/var/tmp) -> \"Graph cache is empty. Query a file or run `hilo graph warm` to populate.\" \u2014 the behavior the row asks for. sha256 5086d8dd3b312196c683223cfe50594606abf068725559d53f44f8bafa132a70.\n- ARM C (branch proof, this host's cache excluded): synthetic ancestor holding ONLY .vfs/graph/edges.jsonl (0 bytes, no manifest), query from its child dir -> \"Graph cache is empty. No edges parsed yet.\" instead of the no-root message, i.e. the ancestor was adopted. The FALLBACK BRANCH fires, not this host's particular cache. sha256 5fd823b5e8477dcac6457c3a5729f3aef2f99e3ada5d8fa114a20e383b50973f.\n\nSEVERITY: silent wrong-scope answer (a foreign tree's census and edge set presented as this directory's graph), an unbounded walk over a 2.5M-file subtree, rc=0, and no line naming which root answered. Users with an initialized project are unaffected; users and tests running anywhere under a directory that merely holds a leftover .vfs/graph are misled. This is also the mechanism behind the QA-WARPFS-029 test-isolation family and compounds QA-WARPFS-037.", "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "attempts": 0, "created_at": "2026-11-11T07:40:42Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T07:53:55Z", "capability_tags": ["qa", "graph", "root-resolution", "ancestor-cache", "false-close", "isolation"], "foreman_note": "cycle:4 warpfs-qa-2026-11-11-04-58-53 corroboration: the adoption is not cosmetic - it breaks the product's OWN test suite. At b345275, same binary, only TMPDIR differs: TMPDIR under $HOME => hilo-cli tests/cli.rs 83/85 (graph_accepts_file_prefixed_path_and_teaches_id_forms, graph_impact_nonexistent_file_errors, graph_stats_no_data_prints_message) and hilo-metadata sidecar::tests::find_workspace_root_none_outside_workspace fail, with graph stats taking 12.0s; TMPDIR=/var/tmp/hermes-scratch (no ancestor .vfs) => 85/85 and 39/39 in 0.01-0.44s. The Binder Error on granularity is symptom of the adopted pre-0.4 cache (tracked separately by QA-WARPFS-037, still pending)."}
