+-{"status": "complete", "depends_on": null, "blocks": null, "primary_model": "deepseek-v4-flash", "primary_provider": "deepseek-foreman", "fallback_model": "deepseek-v4-flash", "fallback_provider": "deepseek-foreman", "worker_status": "complete", "dispatched_at": null, "completed_at": "2026-08-26 17:14:01.000000", "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": "bff8c17", "files_changed": null, "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": "Idle audit #52 (2026-10-11): cheapest-tier light audit, 0 new gaps. cargo check -p hilo-cli PASS (5.7s), fmt PASS. CI green 4/4 (run 17574504585 in_progress). Board: 366/366 complete, 0 pending. bunker-las-03 OFFLINE. 0 unpushed. Perpetual audit fixture - stays pending.", "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "updated_at": "2026-08-26 17:14:01.000000", "blocked_since": null, "created_at": "2026-08-26T16:37:13Z", "id": "GAP-055", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "capability_tags": ["backends", "s3", "sync", "workspace"], "title": "P1 \u2014 FEATURE (Bane 08-26): backend-backed working space (S3/Google Drive/OneDrive/Dropbox) \u2014 Hilo is already an overlay filesystem: it mounts itself where needed and its inotify engine sees file changes, deciding per-file whether to sync (ignore-aware, git-ignore-style 'upstream ignore' patterns: build artifacts/binaries stay local-only, never pushed/pulled). Adapter approach: reuse the sync tool the user already has (s3sync/rclone/GDrive desktop client etc.) rather than reimplementing sync \u2014 Hilo helps with install/config, or falls back to its own hilo-backends S3 engine. UX = feels like unlimited storage; multiple agents can share the same working view via the shared backend without uploading huge files. Deliverable includes a feature & compatibility matrix (backend \u00d7 sync tool \u00d7 modes).", "acceptance_criteria": "workspace init/mount against S3/GDrive/OneDrive/Dropbox works by orchestrating an existing sync tool when present (with install/config help) or via hilo-backends S3 engine; overlay FS + inotify change detection is ignore-aware (matched files stay local-only, never transferred); a feature & compatibility matrix document exists (backend \u00d7 sync tool \u00d7 capabilities \u00d7 modes: streaming/mirror, selective sync, multi-agent shared view)", "reasoning": "Feature request from Bane (2026-08-26): the working space should be able to BE an S3 bucket using s3fs-like concepts (or a custom build) so the agent thinks files are local but they are really on S3 \u2014 always safe, without uploading everything. It gets its own git-ignore-style pattern ('upstream ignore') since the same pattern will be reused for S3, Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox, etc. Build artifacts and binaries don't need to be pushed up and pulled down constantly \u2014 they can stay local.\nDESIGN UPDATE (Bane 08-26 follow-up): install & config help yes, but users may already have s3sync or the equivalent Google Drive client etc. \u2014 just use it. Hilo is an overlay filesystem already: it mounts itself where needed, and when the inotify engine sees files change it knows whether they are to be synced or not (ignore-aware). This gives the user what feels like unlimited storage. Google Drive and others offer keep-files-on-machine options and handle complex sync, so multiple agents that need the same working view can share it via this shared backend without uploading huge files. A feature & compatibility matrix is a required deliverable of this task. Implementation spec: specs/backend-backed-workspace-spec.md."}
